# Always commit tags

When tag definitions change under the Ignition config tree, **always stage and commit them** with the related work. Do not leave tag edits as local-only “scan churn.”

## Include

- `gateways/*/data/config/resources/core/ignition/tag-definition/**`
- `gateways/*/data/config/resources/core/ignition/tag-type-definition/**`
- RCP1 / Plant / Devices / Units UDT and instance files (`tags.json`, `udts.json`, `unary-resource.json`, nested Interlock folders, etc.)

## Exclude (not project tags)

- `tag-definition/System/Gateway/**` StoreAndForward / auditing noise
- Secrets (`.env`, `.ignition-scan.json`)

## Practice

If SIM or config-scan rewrites `udts.json` ↔ `tags.json` + `unary-resource.json`, commit the full consistent set (delete old file + add new + unary) so the repo matches the working gateway.
